This product includes data from the UK Government GHG Conversion Factors for
Company Reporting (pkg/factors/data/desnz-2026.json), published by the
Department for Energy Security and Net Zero.

Contains public sector information licensed under the Open Government Licence v3.0.
https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/

This product includes default emission intensity values (pkg/factors/data/glec-3.3.json,
built by tools/glec/build.py) from: Smart Freight Centre. Global Logistics Emissions
Council Framework for Logistics Emissions Accounting and Reporting; v3.3 edition, revised
and updated (October 2026). ISBN 978-90-833629-0-8. Used with the permission of Smart
Freight Centre, which is acknowledged as the source. No affiliation with or endorsement by
Smart Freight Centre is implied. Smart Freight Centre's copyright notice says the publication
may not be used for resale or any other commercial purpose without its prior written permission.
GLEC credits some of these values to other publications (European fuel factors to
ifeu, INFRAS and Fraunhofer IML; European road values to HBEFA; container trade lanes to
Clean Cargo; North American values to SmartWay and GREET; Ro-Ro to the Global Ro-Ro
Community; hub values to the GILA project of Fraunhofer IML, Politecnico di Milano and
GreenRouter; European rail load factors, empty running and electric train energy, Indian
upstream electricity and one intermodal terminal value to EcoTransIT World); they are
included as GLEC publishes them.
Country continents for the GLEC regions (tools/glec/countries.csv) are from OurAirports,
public domain.

This product includes electricity carbon intensity data
(pkg/factors/data/grid/ember-owid.json) from Ember, Yearly Electricity Data,
processed by Our World in Data (https://github.com/owid/energy-data).
Licensed under CC BY 4.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

This product includes inland waterway emission factors
(pkg/factors/data/nl-iww-2026.json) from the Dutch CO2 emission factor list,
www.co2emissiefactoren.nl (2026), based on CE Delft (2021), STREAM
Goederenvervoer, Emissies van modaliteiten in het goederenvervoer 2020,
versie 2. Source: www.co2emissiefactoren.nl
No terms of use for the list were found; permission to redistribute it has not been
confirmed.

This product includes container ship emission factors (pkg/factors/data/eu-mrv-2024.json,
generated by tools/mrv) calculated from EU MRV data (Regulation (EU) 2015/757), reporting
period 2024, published by the European Maritime Safety Agency (THETIS-MRV).
Source: European Maritime Safety Agency (EMSA). EMSA allows reproduction as long as the
source is acknowledged.

This product includes place data (pkg/places/data/places.tsv.gz):
- cities from GeoNames (https://www.geonames.org), licensed under CC BY 4.0:
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
- UN/LOCODE, the United Nations Code for Trade and Transport Locations, maintained
  by UNECE (https://unece.org/trade/uncefact/unlocode), via the datasets/un-locode
  package (https://github.com/datasets/un-locode). UNECE's terms for UN/LOCODE are
  unclear: the UN/LOCODE site's terms of use allow personal, non-commercial use without
  redistribution, while the same site says UN/CEFACT standards are free to use under
  CC BY 4.0. Permission to redistribute has not been confirmed.
- airports from OurAirports (https://ourairports.com), public domain

Country borders (pkg/borders/data/borders.bin.gz, built by tools/borders) are Natural
Earth's 1:10m admin-0 countries, v5.1.2 (https://www.naturalearthdata.com), public domain.

Map tiles and routing data: (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, under the Open Database
License (https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright). They are not bundled; the map tiles are
loaded from openstreetmap.org and the routing graphs are built where Sootcase is deployed.
The maritime network, Eurostat SeaRoute (EUPL-1.2), is not bundled either.

